1
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:12,125
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

2
00:00:12,221 --> 00:00:14,061
Street Restaurant Fighter.

3
00:00:14,068 --> 00:00:17,134
(Final mission, Everyone's Restaurant)

4
00:00:17,192 --> 00:00:19,732
(Jung Ho Young and Song Hoon's new restaurant)

5
00:00:19,732 --> 00:00:22,262
(Noodle Shop of Brothers with Different-sized Stomachs)

6
00:00:22,262 --> 00:00:25,172
(Competing with their signature pasta and udon)

7
00:00:25,172 --> 00:00:27,542
(Lee Sung Hoon and Yu Tae Hee)

8
00:00:27,842 --> 00:00:29,442
(Competing with a 7-course menu...)

9
00:00:29,442 --> 00:00:31,842
(to maximize the average spending per customer)

10
00:00:32,012 --> 00:00:35,982
(Kim Hoon and Kim Jong In)

11
00:00:35,982 --> 00:00:39,612
(Competing with mainstream dishes that are hard to dislike)

12
00:00:40,552 --> 00:00:44,222
(1st target: 32 competitors who came in as customers)

13
00:00:44,352 --> 00:00:48,492
(Attracting the attention of dining chefs with a full-course menu)

14
00:00:48,562 --> 00:00:50,262
(Current total number of customers)

15
00:00:50,262 --> 00:00:51,692
(Lee Sung Hoon 16, Jung Ho Young 8, Kim Hoon 8)

16
00:00:52,292 --> 00:00:56,462
Next, around 20 people working in the restaurant industry...

17
00:00:56,462 --> 00:00:58,732
- in Jeonju will enter.
- What did she say?

18
00:00:58,732 --> 00:01:00,862
About 20 people working in the restaurant industry...

19
00:01:00,862 --> 00:01:02,062
in Jeonju.

20
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:03,062
Okay.

21
00:01:03,062 --> 00:01:04,132
(25 professionals in Jeonju restaurant industry)

22
00:01:04,132 --> 00:01:05,332
We must be eating inside.

23
00:01:06,853 --> 00:01:08,893
- Are we going in?
- I think we're eating inside.

24
00:01:08,893 --> 00:01:09,953
(Except for the part-timers, the contestants can't come out.)

25
00:01:10,563 --> 00:01:12,463
- There's a menu here too.
- There's tenderloin steak.

26
00:01:13,723 --> 00:01:17,163
(Lee Sung Hoon's course menu catches their attention right away.)

27
00:01:17,193 --> 00:01:18,563
Is this really 34 dollars?

28
00:01:20,533 --> 00:01:23,273
- A course meal?
- Is it not just the main dish?

29
00:01:24,543 --> 00:01:26,103
- In that case, - How is this possible?

30
00:01:26,103 --> 00:01:27,473
that's good value for money.

31
00:01:27,473 --> 00:01:28,773
(Thinking)

32
00:01:28,943 --> 00:01:29,943
Let's go with the course meal.

33
00:01:31,443 --> 00:01:32,643
(Their first choice is Lee Sung Hoon.)

34
00:01:32,643 --> 00:01:33,713
This is the best.

35
00:01:33,983 --> 00:01:36,583
- Hello.
- Hello.

36
00:01:36,583 --> 00:01:38,623
Please go inside and take a seat.

37
00:01:38,683 --> 00:01:39,753
No matter how good it tastes,

38
00:01:40,053 --> 00:01:42,153
- pork cutlet is just pork cutlet.
- Right.

39
00:01:42,153 --> 00:01:43,723
- I'll go here.
- Me too.

40
00:01:43,723 --> 00:01:44,763
I'm drawn to this.

41
00:01:45,323 --> 00:01:46,363
(Jeonju restaurant industry professionals, 9 out of 25)

42
00:01:46,363 --> 00:01:47,863
- Hello.
- Hello.

43
00:01:48,593 --> 00:01:50,063
What's going on at this restaurant?

44
00:01:50,903 --> 00:01:54,533
- People keep coming in.
- People are flocking here.

45
00:01:55,133 --> 00:01:56,533
- What shall we eat?
- This is insane.

46
00:01:57,803 --> 00:01:59,303
Hello.

47
00:01:59,303 --> 00:02:00,573
(The customers keep coming in one after the other.)

48
00:02:01,073 --> 00:02:02,943
- Is there no table?
- What should we do? We're three.

49
00:02:02,943 --> 00:02:05,543
You have to write down your name on the waiting list.

50
00:02:05,543 --> 00:02:06,613
Thank you.

51
00:02:07,451 --> 00:02:08,511
Are you going to wait for it?

52
00:02:09,151 --> 00:02:10,681
I think this place is...

53
00:02:11,121 --> 00:02:12,351
worth waiting for.

54
00:02:12,351 --> 00:02:14,721
It's impossible to eat this at this price.

55
00:02:14,721 --> 00:02:15,791
I know.

56
00:02:16,351 --> 00:02:17,891
- Is it the price per person?
- Yes.

57
00:02:17,891 --> 00:02:18,991
Even if it is...

58
00:02:20,461 --> 00:02:22,131
It's completely packed now.

59
00:02:23,031 --> 00:02:25,331
- Have a drink while you wait.
- Thank you.

60
00:02:25,331 --> 00:02:26,431
(Lee Sung Hoon's Son of Jeonju is full.)

61
00:02:26,431 --> 00:02:29,471
(17 out of 25 Jeonju restaurant industry professionals picked it.)

62
00:02:29,701 --> 00:02:31,701
(Current total number of customers)

63
00:02:31,701 --> 00:02:34,341
(Lee Sung Hoon firmly holds on to 1st place.)

64
00:02:34,611 --> 00:02:37,041
(Black pork tenderloin steak grilled over charcoal piece by piece)

65
00:02:37,271 --> 00:02:40,211
(The charcoal-grilled dish needs to be cooked low and slow.)

66
00:02:40,281 --> 00:02:42,981
(A secret technique to cut down on cooking time)

67
00:02:43,281 --> 00:02:45,251
- How many minutes remain?
- Twenty minutes.

68
00:02:45,251 --> 00:02:46,281
(Meat partially cooked in advance before service)

69
00:02:46,281 --> 00:02:47,321
That will work.

70
00:02:48,491 --> 00:02:50,391
(By using the sous vide method that cooks the meat slowly...)

71
00:02:50,391 --> 00:02:51,691
(at a low temperature,)

72
00:02:51,961 --> 00:02:55,431
(Lee Sung Hoon manages to save both time and flavour.)

73
00:02:55,831 --> 00:02:58,661
(With the steak that's cooked by 80 percent)

74
00:02:59,901 --> 00:03:02,631
I was going to make a tare sauce, dip the steak in it for a moment,

75
00:03:03,271 --> 00:03:06,671
and then cook it quickly over the charcoal.

76
00:03:14,681 --> 00:03:16,751
It looks good. It's perfect.

77
00:03:17,951 --> 00:03:19,821
What else goes on the dish?

78
00:03:20,521 --> 00:03:22,091
- Napa cabbage.
- Napa cabbage.

79
00:03:24,821 --> 00:03:25,991
(Salted anchovies, grilled napa cabbage, carrot puree)

80
00:03:25,991 --> 00:03:29,331
(The 4th course dish, Jeju black pork tenderloin steak)

81
00:03:30,391 --> 00:03:32,431
Here's for one person. I'll bring you another side plate.

82
00:03:32,431 --> 00:03:33,501
Okay.

83
00:03:33,501 --> 00:03:35,501
(Starting with the meat)

84
00:03:35,501 --> 00:03:38,701
(Staring)

85
00:03:38,971 --> 00:03:40,841
How can you eat the cabbage without a knife?

86
00:03:41,441 --> 00:03:43,811
(Napa cabbage with the stem still attached)

87
00:03:44,071 --> 00:03:45,341
I'll cut it.

88
00:03:46,081 --> 00:03:47,411
Should I cut it like kimchi?

89
00:03:47,651 --> 00:03:48,711
That's a great idea.

90
00:03:49,111 --> 00:03:51,651
(Tearing with his hands)

91
00:03:53,681 --> 00:03:54,751
Is that for me?

92
00:03:54,751 --> 00:03:56,051
(Chan Hee, the baby bird)

93
00:03:56,051 --> 00:03:57,921
Are you going to eat my finger too?

94
00:03:59,591 --> 00:04:02,361
Think about cutting off the cabbage stem. There are no knives.

95
00:04:02,491 --> 00:04:04,201
I got it.

96
00:04:04,201 --> 00:04:05,661
(Ho Yoon gives feedback after witnessing an unpleasant scene.)

97
00:04:06,501 --> 00:04:09,501
(Cutting off the stem)

98
00:04:09,771 --> 00:04:11,871
I told them to cut off the stem.

99
00:04:13,571 --> 00:04:15,611
(A bite of the meat)

100
00:04:16,371 --> 00:04:17,681
It's really good.

101
00:04:18,881 --> 00:04:20,011
It has no porky smell at all.

102
00:04:21,111 --> 00:04:24,251
Here's your steak and Korean melon salad.

103
00:04:24,251 --> 00:04:25,381
- Is this...
- Excuse me.

104
00:04:25,651 --> 00:04:26,981
They're served together.

105
00:04:27,321 --> 00:04:29,551
Isn't it served with cucumber and onions?

106
00:04:30,721 --> 00:04:32,761
(The 5th course dish, sweet corn Korean melon salad)

107
00:04:32,761 --> 00:04:35,261
(Beet, Korean melon, cucumber, onion, dill, sweet corn)

108
00:04:35,531 --> 00:04:38,701
(Starting with the salad)

109
00:04:39,331 --> 00:04:41,271
(Taking another bite)

110
00:04:41,271 --> 00:04:42,901
(Nodding)

111
00:04:42,901 --> 00:04:45,201
(Next is the main dish.)

112
00:04:45,301 --> 00:04:46,501
Is this puree?

113
00:04:46,501 --> 00:04:48,071
Carrot puree?

114
00:04:49,371 --> 00:04:50,471
The carrot puree is good.

115
00:04:52,481 --> 00:04:54,751
(A bite of the meat)

116
00:04:54,951 --> 00:04:57,351
(Humming with approval)

117
00:04:58,221 --> 00:05:03,891
(This time, he wraps the meat with the napa cabbage.)

118
00:05:05,061 --> 00:05:07,291
(Turning around)

119
00:05:08,991 --> 00:05:10,861
- May I get some salt?
- Salt?

120
00:05:10,861 --> 00:05:12,601
- Just a bit of salt.
- Could you give me salt?

121
00:05:13,131 --> 00:05:14,601
- I'm sorry.
- Which one is too bland?

122
00:05:14,631 --> 00:05:16,231
- What?
- Which one is bland for you?

123
00:05:17,231 --> 00:05:18,771
- The napa cabbage.
- The napa cabbage?

124
00:05:18,771 --> 00:05:20,471
- Please tell him.
- Okay.

125
00:05:20,471 --> 00:05:22,211
- There's no seasoning...
- It should be stronger?

126
00:05:22,211 --> 00:05:24,071
to the napa cabbage.

127
00:05:24,441 --> 00:05:27,781
It'd be fine if it were seasoned,

128
00:05:27,781 --> 00:05:29,581
but there's barely any seasoning.

129
00:05:29,581 --> 00:05:31,051
- But the food is delicious.
- Thank you.

130
00:05:31,051 --> 00:05:32,621
Also, the salad needs more seasoning.

131
00:05:33,351 --> 00:05:35,591
We shouldn't be giving our opinions.

132
00:05:35,791 --> 00:05:37,761
If everyone here starts giving their two cents...

133
00:05:38,421 --> 00:05:40,761
We need to stop Chef Edward Kwon.

134
00:05:40,761 --> 00:05:42,091
The chef needs to block it all out.

135
00:05:42,931 --> 00:05:44,431
Thank you, chef.

136
00:05:46,201 --> 00:05:48,371
The napa cabbage is a little too bland.

137
00:05:48,371 --> 00:05:50,071
It'd be better with some salt.

138
00:05:50,071 --> 00:05:51,841
- Okay.
- For the Korean melon salad,

139
00:05:51,971 --> 00:05:54,711
- it's a little...
- Don't listen too much...

140
00:05:54,711 --> 00:05:56,141
to what other people are saying.

141
00:05:56,311 --> 00:05:57,911
- Okay.
- Don't be swayed by them.

142
00:05:58,641 --> 00:06:00,641
He shouldn't stop the part-timer like that.

143
00:06:00,641 --> 00:06:02,751
- No way.
- That's not what I meant.

144
00:06:03,111 --> 00:06:04,851
I meant to stop the other chefs.

145
00:06:05,781 --> 00:06:08,191
Only fix service-related issues that can cause inconvenience.

146
00:06:08,191 --> 00:06:09,321
No, he shouldn't say that either.

147
00:06:09,321 --> 00:06:11,021
People need to stop going to the kitchen.

148
00:06:11,561 --> 00:06:13,761
(Ho Yoon comes back after giving feedback.)

149
00:06:13,761 --> 00:06:15,331
(This time, it's Seok Cheon's turn.)

150
00:06:15,331 --> 00:06:16,791
Seok Cheon, what's this?

151
00:06:18,061 --> 00:06:20,331
- What?
- I was just trying to stop you.

152
00:06:20,331 --> 00:06:21,701
- What is it?
- It's nothing.

153
00:06:21,931 --> 00:06:23,301
Everything is solved.

154
00:06:23,301 --> 00:06:24,971
He was trying to stop you from going in there.

155
00:06:25,071 --> 00:06:27,141
Everyone is giving their opinion.

156
00:06:28,241 --> 00:06:29,571
I was stopping you from going in.

157
00:06:30,541 --> 00:06:34,041
(At Jung Ho Young's noodle shop next door)

158
00:06:34,911 --> 00:06:36,251
May I come in?

159
00:06:36,251 --> 00:06:37,981
- Yes, of course.
- Okay.

160
00:06:37,981 --> 00:06:39,381
Hello.

161
00:06:39,381 --> 00:06:41,091
(1 restaurant industry professional)

162
00:06:41,645 --> 00:06:42,745
Hello.

163
00:06:43,175 --> 00:06:45,445
Hello. Take a seat wherever you'd like.

164
00:06:45,445 --> 00:06:47,145
(8 restaurant industry professionals)

165
00:06:47,615 --> 00:06:50,985
(8 Jeonju restaurant industry professionals came in.)

166
00:06:51,315 --> 00:06:53,415
- Are you here by yourself?
- Yes.

167
00:06:53,585 --> 00:06:55,185
- Could you sit together?
- Sure.

168
00:06:55,185 --> 00:06:57,255
- I was kidding.
- I would be glad to.

169
00:06:57,255 --> 00:06:58,895
- Aren't you bored alone?
- Yes.

170
00:06:59,695 --> 00:07:02,295
This way, you get to know each other.

171
00:07:02,295 --> 00:07:03,465
What would you like?

172
00:07:03,895 --> 00:07:06,265
I'd like one fresh pasta...

173
00:07:06,265 --> 00:07:07,665
and sushi, please.

174
00:07:07,665 --> 00:07:08,735
- Sushi?
- Yes.

175
00:07:08,735 --> 00:07:10,935
We have soy sauce over here.

176
00:07:11,335 --> 00:07:14,375
Please feel free to serve yourself.

177
00:07:15,805 --> 00:07:17,375
I'll take some wet tissue for us.

178
00:07:19,375 --> 00:07:20,615
Thank you.

179
00:07:20,615 --> 00:07:23,745
(They got close enough to serve each other soy sauce with vinegar.)

180
00:07:24,145 --> 00:07:25,815
Do you work in the restaurant industry in Jeonju?

181
00:07:25,815 --> 00:07:28,025
- Yes.
- May I ask what you do?

182
00:07:28,255 --> 00:07:30,625
I don't run a restaurant.

183
00:07:30,625 --> 00:07:32,455
- I run a cafe over there.
- I see.

184
00:07:32,455 --> 00:07:34,095
- At Jeonju Hanok Village?
- Yes.

185
00:07:34,495 --> 00:07:36,265
- Do you run a restaurant?
- Yes.

186
00:07:36,265 --> 00:07:38,235
I run a franchise. We serve...

187
00:07:38,235 --> 00:07:40,335
- gimbap wrapped in grilled meat.
- Is it Restaurant O?

188
00:07:40,335 --> 00:07:41,965
It's one of the branches.

189
00:07:41,965 --> 00:07:43,965
- Is it a branch?
- Yes.

190
00:07:44,375 --> 00:07:46,035
I think we're around the same age.

191
00:07:46,035 --> 00:07:48,105
- I was born in 1989.
- Me too.

192
00:07:48,305 --> 00:07:50,705
We're the same age. And we ran into each other.

193
00:07:50,705 --> 00:07:51,845
(What a small world)

194
00:07:52,145 --> 00:07:54,245
- Here's your pasta.
- Thank you.

195
00:07:54,545 --> 00:07:55,785
- They make the set menu.
- I see.

196
00:07:55,785 --> 00:07:57,315
- These two?
- Yes.

197
00:07:57,855 --> 00:07:59,085
Enjoy your food.

198
00:07:59,085 --> 00:08:01,025
I've never seen a bowl this big.

199
00:08:02,055 --> 00:08:04,755
I can feel how chewy the noodles are with my chopsticks.

200
00:08:09,265 --> 00:08:13,095
(After slurping it in,)

201
00:08:13,095 --> 00:08:15,665
(he studies the menu carefully.)

202
00:08:16,535 --> 00:08:18,575
Did he make the noodles himself?

203
00:08:19,235 --> 00:08:20,405
No way.

204
00:08:21,005 --> 00:08:22,805
- The noodles are nice and chewy.
- Yes.

205
00:08:25,315 --> 00:08:28,085
- Try some seafood.
- Thank you.

206
00:08:28,785 --> 00:08:30,615
It's nice that we ended up sitting together...

207
00:08:30,615 --> 00:08:31,955
and sharing the food.

208
00:08:33,085 --> 00:08:35,455
I'll buy us shaved ice. Would you like to try some?

209
00:08:35,455 --> 00:08:36,825
Besides, you run a cafe.

210
00:08:37,755 --> 00:08:41,295
I was thinking of ordering one too.

211
00:08:41,625 --> 00:08:42,825
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

212
00:08:42,825 --> 00:08:45,565
Can we order shaved ice right now?

213
00:08:45,565 --> 00:08:47,665
Of course. Why not?

214
00:08:48,405 --> 00:08:51,005
(The noodle shop's dessert, snowflake shaved ice)

215
00:08:51,175 --> 00:08:53,235
(Finely shaved milk ice)

216
00:08:54,075 --> 00:08:56,845
(Loaded with sweet red beans)

217
00:08:56,845 --> 00:08:58,515
(Shaved ice rice cakes)

218
00:08:58,515 --> 00:09:00,145
(Injeolmi powder)

219
00:09:00,145 --> 00:09:02,785
(Condensed milk)

220
00:09:03,045 --> 00:09:04,115
(Snowflake shaved ice that stays true to the basics)

221
00:09:04,115 --> 00:09:05,615
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

222
00:09:05,615 --> 00:09:07,615
- Did you get to know each other?
- Yes, we're best friends now.

223
00:09:08,525 --> 00:09:10,155
Shaved ice is quite expensive these days,

224
00:09:10,155 --> 00:09:12,655
but 6.50 dollars feels very affordable.

225
00:09:12,995 --> 00:09:15,125
You're right about the price.

226
00:09:15,165 --> 00:09:17,735
Even a cup of shaved ice costs around five dollars.

227
00:09:18,465 --> 00:09:20,595
Considering that it's only 6.50 dollars,

228
00:09:20,595 --> 00:09:22,105
- Right?
- it's a great deal.

229
00:09:22,105 --> 00:09:24,305
It's nice to take care of the dessert in one spot.

230
00:09:25,275 --> 00:09:28,105
(Meanwhile, customers waiting at Son of Jeonju)

231
00:09:28,175 --> 00:09:30,175
It looks like most people went into these two restaurants.

232
00:09:30,175 --> 00:09:31,575
Hardly anyone went in there.

233
00:09:32,045 --> 00:09:34,315
- The menu feels too everyday.
- Everyday?

234
00:09:34,315 --> 00:09:35,815
It'd be a waste to eat here.

235
00:09:37,445 --> 00:09:40,155
Also, the menu items are too common.

236
00:09:40,585 --> 00:09:42,025
They may appeal to the general public, but...

237
00:09:43,825 --> 00:09:46,225
Don't you feel down because there's no music?

238
00:09:46,455 --> 00:09:48,865
- Since there's no music...
- No music at the restaurant.

239
00:09:50,265 --> 00:09:52,995
It means that no one came to our restaurant.

240
00:09:57,935 --> 00:09:59,575
This is depressing. I guess they went to Jung Ho Young's shop.

241
00:10:01,005 --> 00:10:03,445
The restaurant professionals and the general public...

242
00:10:03,445 --> 00:10:05,115
- will have different tastes.
- Right.

243
00:10:07,015 --> 00:10:09,945
The second target group that's coming in next is...

244
00:10:10,791 --> 00:10:12,091
senior citizens.

245
00:10:13,161 --> 00:10:14,661
Are we eating right away?

246
00:10:15,431 --> 00:10:17,401
(Average age is 70.)

247
00:10:17,401 --> 00:10:20,131
After eating the food, we have to give feedback...

248
00:10:20,131 --> 00:10:21,541
and mark our choice.

249
00:10:21,701 --> 00:10:24,171
I guess we eat at one place and evaluate the food.

250
00:10:24,571 --> 00:10:26,411
Whether the food was prepared properly or not.

251
00:10:26,571 --> 00:10:27,711
Whether it's good or not.

252
00:10:29,041 --> 00:10:30,481
This will become a memory.

253
00:10:30,711 --> 00:10:32,181
Of course.

254
00:10:34,151 --> 00:10:35,851
What shall we eat?

255
00:10:37,221 --> 00:10:39,391
- Senior citizens...
- Senior citizens like sushi.

256
00:10:39,551 --> 00:10:40,951
Sushi or udon would be strong choices.

257
00:10:41,521 --> 00:10:42,891
They wouldn't go for lasagna.

258
00:10:44,191 --> 00:10:45,291
- Would the seniors...
- Would the seniors...

259
00:10:45,291 --> 00:10:46,361
choose the course menu?

260
00:10:46,361 --> 00:10:47,731
I don't think so.

261
00:10:47,961 --> 00:10:49,361
For some reason,

262
00:10:50,401 --> 00:10:51,831
I think they'd go for pork cutlet.

263
00:10:52,501 --> 00:10:55,901
- It must be a noodle shop.
- Noodles?

264
00:10:55,901 --> 00:10:58,611
They have different types of noodles.

265
