Most of them are noodles.

266
00:11:00,711 --> 00:11:02,641
- Pick what you want.
- I don't want noodles.

267
00:11:03,781 --> 00:11:06,311
They have noodles here.

268
00:11:07,311 --> 00:11:09,351
From the look of it, there isn't much for me to eat.

269
00:11:10,181 --> 00:11:11,721
That one is expensive.

270
00:11:11,921 --> 00:11:14,291
It's calamari and shrimp fresh pasta.

271
00:11:14,421 --> 00:11:15,991
Pasta isn't good.

272
00:11:17,121 --> 00:11:19,331
We should eat rice. They sell food made with flour.

273
00:11:19,691 --> 00:11:23,061
It's 35 dollars? It's very expensive.

274
00:11:23,661 --> 00:11:26,171
A chef from Jeonju?

275
00:11:27,101 --> 00:11:29,141
It must be a course meal.

276
00:11:30,071 --> 00:11:32,111
It's expensive because it's a course meal.

277
00:11:33,171 --> 00:11:34,371
Everything is expensive here.

278
00:11:35,711 --> 00:11:38,651
- Let's just go in anywhere.
- Which one?

279
00:11:40,751 --> 00:11:43,351
Pork cutlets. Does that sound okay?

280
00:11:44,991 --> 00:11:46,621
Handmade jumbo pork cutlet.

281
00:11:46,621 --> 00:11:48,421
(Handmade jumbo pork cutlet)

282
00:11:49,221 --> 00:11:50,891
(Glancing at the door)

283
00:11:51,691 --> 00:11:53,131
Why isn't anyone coming to our restaurant?

284
00:11:55,501 --> 00:11:58,431
(The current situation at Jung Ho Young's Noodle Shop)

285
00:11:58,531 --> 00:12:01,901
(The current situation at Lee Sung Hoon's Son of Jeonju)

286
00:12:02,041 --> 00:12:03,841
Which one looks the best?

287
00:12:04,301 --> 00:12:05,711
I'll go to this one.

288
00:12:06,141 --> 00:12:08,911
- Jumbo pork cutlet?
- Yes.

289
00:12:09,211 --> 00:12:10,781
- Are you getting a pork cutlet?
- Yes.

290
00:12:11,351 --> 00:12:12,681
Okay, let's get that.

291
00:12:13,881 --> 00:12:15,781
- This looks delicious.
- I agree.

292
00:12:16,051 --> 00:12:17,421
- How about this?
- This looks the best.

293
00:12:17,421 --> 00:12:19,891
Let's try this one.

294
00:12:20,051 --> 00:12:21,221
Gambas are delicious.

295
00:12:21,221 --> 00:12:22,821
Also, the ice cream is free.

296
00:12:24,161 --> 00:12:26,591
The soba is cheap. It's only 2.90 dollars.

297
00:12:29,131 --> 00:12:31,131
- Welcome. Nice to meet you.
- Welcome.

298
00:12:31,131 --> 00:12:32,201
Hello.

299
00:12:32,201 --> 00:12:34,231
- Two people?
- Welcome.

300
00:12:34,231 --> 00:12:35,501
Please follow me.

301
00:12:35,641 --> 00:12:36,871
(Seoul Jumbo Pork Cutlet and Hamburger Steak receive...)

302
00:12:36,871 --> 00:12:38,111
(the first senior citizen customers.)

303
00:12:38,441 --> 00:12:40,771
- I'll take your order. Welcome.
- Welcome.

304
00:12:40,771 --> 00:12:42,111
Please be careful.

305
00:12:42,411 --> 00:12:43,981
Watch your step.

306
00:12:43,981 --> 00:12:45,611
- We need to watch our step.
- Please come in.

307
00:12:45,811 --> 00:12:47,981
You don't have to write that. Just come in.

308
00:12:48,364 --> 00:12:50,394
Please come in. Welcome.

309
00:12:50,864 --> 00:12:52,364
Welcome.

310
00:12:53,194 --> 00:12:54,934
How many are you?

311
00:12:55,934 --> 00:12:57,534
Welcome. How many are you?

312
00:12:57,534 --> 00:12:58,634
I'll put it on for you.

313
00:12:58,634 --> 00:13:00,574
- Feel free to sit anywhere.
- Hello.

314
00:13:00,904 --> 00:13:02,004
Okay.

315
00:13:02,004 --> 00:13:04,074
- You have to sit somewhere else.
- Okay.

316
00:13:04,144 --> 00:13:05,514
Thank you. A lot of people are coming in.

317
00:13:06,814 --> 00:13:08,944
(The restaurant gets packed in no time.)

318
00:13:13,054 --> 00:13:14,824
Everyone rushed into the pork cutlet place.

319
00:13:14,824 --> 00:13:16,024
I knew it.

320
00:13:16,354 --> 00:13:18,494
Let's go, pork cutlet.

321
00:13:18,854 --> 00:13:22,494
(When the door opens,)

322
00:13:22,494 --> 00:13:26,164
(endless senior citizens come in.)

323
00:13:26,164 --> 00:13:27,264
Pork cutlet?

324
00:13:27,564 --> 00:13:30,064
All the senior citizens went into the pork cutlet place.

325
00:13:30,634 --> 00:13:32,104
All of them went in.

326
00:13:32,104 --> 00:13:33,834
The pork cutlet shop turned everything around in one shot.

327
00:13:33,834 --> 00:13:34,904
- What?
- My gosh.

328
00:13:34,944 --> 00:13:36,304
- Pork cutlet.
- Goodness.

329
00:13:36,904 --> 00:13:38,514
- Oh, my.
- Senior citizens.

330
00:13:38,514 --> 00:13:40,514
The senior citizens must've chosen it for the price.

331
00:13:40,844 --> 00:13:42,744
- It's because of the price.
- The price.

332
00:13:43,044 --> 00:13:44,814
(The dining area is packed.)

333
00:13:44,814 --> 00:13:46,384
Thank you.

334
00:13:48,124 --> 00:13:49,254
(Smiling)

335
00:13:49,254 --> 00:13:50,324
I'm sorry.

336
00:13:50,524 --> 00:13:51,524
Jong In.

337
00:13:51,994 --> 00:13:53,824
Jong In, we have to cook at least ten pork cutlets.

338
00:13:54,254 --> 00:13:56,824
- Are you okay?
- Yes, I'm fine. I'll do it.

339
00:13:57,824 --> 00:14:00,394
I thought they'd go to Chef Song Hoon's.

340
00:14:00,394 --> 00:14:01,404
Same here.

341
00:14:01,404 --> 00:14:04,204
But everyone ended up here and not Chef Song Hoon's.

342
00:14:04,674 --> 00:14:05,974
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

343
00:14:05,974 --> 00:14:07,534
You're much more handsome in real life.

344
00:14:07,534 --> 00:14:08,544
Thank you.

345
00:14:08,544 --> 00:14:10,704
(There are only two tables of elderly at Jung Ho Young's.)

346
00:14:12,544 --> 00:14:15,514
I'm worried we don't have many customers.

347
00:14:18,714 --> 00:14:21,184
Among the second target group,

348
00:14:21,824 --> 00:14:23,024
about 40 elderly customers...

349
00:14:23,724 --> 00:14:27,354
have entered Seoul Jumbo Pork Cutlet and Hamburger Steak.

350
00:14:27,794 --> 00:14:28,864
Forty customers?

351
00:14:31,094 --> 00:14:33,094
Forty went to Seoul Jumbo Pork Cutlet and Hamburger Steak.

352
00:14:33,094 --> 00:14:34,534
What a big surprise.

353
00:14:34,534 --> 00:14:35,904
Is it a group? Did a tourist bus stop nearby?

354
00:14:36,104 --> 00:14:38,104
- Let's all go there.
- Is there a group tour?

355
00:14:41,644 --> 00:14:44,914
(With Kim Hoon taking 90 percent of the 2nd target group)

356
00:14:45,144 --> 00:14:48,214
Here's the current sales ranking.

357
00:14:49,144 --> 00:14:51,714
In first place, Lee Sung Hoon and Yu Tae Hee...

358
00:14:52,054 --> 00:14:53,584
with 1,122 dollars.

359
00:14:54,084 --> 00:14:56,524
In second place, Kim Hoon and Kim Jong In...

360
00:14:56,854 --> 00:14:58,624
with 805.80 dollars.

361
00:14:59,124 --> 00:15:01,624
In third place, Jung Ho Young and Song Hoon...

362
00:15:01,964 --> 00:15:03,524
with 757 dollars.

363
00:15:04,664 --> 00:15:05,764
It's a nip-and-tuck match between the two.

364
00:15:05,764 --> 00:15:07,564
The thing is, there was a rush of customers.

365
00:15:09,434 --> 00:15:11,004
It's hard to even guess.

366
00:15:11,304 --> 00:15:13,574
How's it going right now? We're losing, right?

367
00:15:13,574 --> 00:15:15,144
- We're in last place.
- Last place?

368
00:15:15,144 --> 00:15:16,174
Yes, last place.

369
00:15:17,904 --> 00:15:19,044
Is there a huge gap?

370
00:15:19,314 --> 00:15:21,214
We're 100-something dollars behind 2nd place.

371
00:15:22,484 --> 00:15:23,484
Is it that restaurant?

372
00:15:23,484 --> 00:15:26,384
The word "Seoul" does sell.

373
00:15:29,454 --> 00:15:30,754
If you're ready to order,

374
00:15:30,754 --> 00:15:32,824
