492
00:19:59,124 --> 00:20:03,024
The meat is savoury. It tastes savoury.

493
00:20:05,434 --> 00:20:07,064
The portion is huge.

494
00:20:08,704 --> 00:20:10,734
I didn't think I'd have my first soba of the year here.

495
00:20:11,134 --> 00:20:13,304
(Laughing)

496
00:20:14,974 --> 00:20:19,714
(The two elders share their dishes.)

497
00:20:19,714 --> 00:20:20,774
It's good.

498
00:20:21,944 --> 00:20:24,244
Take a lot. I'm only going to eat a little.

499
00:20:24,514 --> 00:20:25,554
No.

500
00:20:25,554 --> 00:20:27,214
Don't say no to me. Dig in, okay?

501
00:20:27,654 --> 00:20:29,824
It's the kind of food you like.

502
00:20:30,084 --> 00:20:31,754
This is what you eat overseas.

503
00:20:32,254 --> 00:20:34,324
(Laughing)

504
00:20:34,594 --> 00:20:36,264
- I find it delicious.
- Right?

505
00:20:38,024 --> 00:20:39,364
The pork cutlet isn't bad.

506
00:20:39,534 --> 00:20:41,264
- What?
- The pork cutlet isn't bad.

507
00:20:41,904 --> 00:20:43,004
How is it?

508
00:20:43,434 --> 00:20:44,504
It's good.

509
00:20:45,504 --> 00:20:47,634
(Skilled with the knife)

510
00:20:50,344 --> 00:20:53,344
Turns out the elderly customers really like pork cutlets.

511
00:20:53,614 --> 00:20:54,644
You never know.

512
00:20:54,644 --> 00:20:57,244
Menus that people are familiar with might be a hit.

513
00:20:57,244 --> 00:20:59,714
How much we brainstorm and such doesn't matter.

514
00:20:59,984 --> 00:21:01,254
The food has to be good, served fast, warm,

515
00:21:01,254 --> 00:21:02,554
and generous in portion!

516
00:21:02,684 --> 00:21:04,084
- The end.
- That must be what business is.

