00:53:30,114 --> 00:53:32,414
If I were an office worker in Jeonju,

1297
00:53:32,414 --> 00:53:34,724
I'd want to splurge a little today.

1298
00:53:35,524 --> 00:53:37,424
Lee Sung Hoon and Yu Tae Hee...

1299
00:53:37,424 --> 00:53:40,054
chose office workers as their main target.

1300
00:53:41,264 --> 00:53:44,334
Actually, a seven-course meal easily costs...

1301
00:53:44,334 --> 00:53:46,494
at least 70 dollars these days,

1302
00:53:46,834 --> 00:53:49,504
but since ours is half that price,

1303
00:53:49,634 --> 00:53:51,434
they'd think, "Let's treat ourselves to a course meal this time."

1304
00:53:51,874 --> 00:53:54,804
And I thought office workers, who are relatively well-off,

1305
00:53:54,804 --> 00:53:57,574
would really appreciate that.

1306
00:53:58,514 --> 00:54:02,314
(Which restaurant will the office workers choose?)

1307
00:54:07,224 --> 00:54:10,824
(Heading straight for the Son of Jeonju)

1308
00:54:10,824 --> 00:54:12,024
It's a course meal.

1309
00:54:12,194 --> 00:54:13,394
And the food looks pretty good.

1310
00:54:15,424 --> 00:54:17,634
The catch is, it's 34 dollars here.

1311
00:54:18,894 --> 00:54:21,364
Even if we went somewhere else,

1312
00:54:22,034 --> 00:54:23,534
we'd probably end up spending 50 to 60 dollars anyway.

1313
00:54:23,874 --> 00:54:26,174
(Waiting)

1314
00:54:26,304 --> 00:54:28,104
Rather than something casual,

1315
00:54:28,404 --> 00:54:30,374
they'd want to spend a bit of money since it's dinner.

1316
00:54:31,044 --> 00:54:32,174
Are you going to eat here?

1317
00:54:32,644 --> 00:54:33,944
I'm torn.

1318
00:54:33,944 --> 00:54:34,944
(Son of Jeonju)

1319
00:54:34,944 --> 00:54:36,014
You can't eat food like this anywhere else.

1320
00:54:36,014 --> 00:54:37,084
Okay.

1321
00:54:37,354 --> 00:54:39,654
(Waiting)

1322
00:54:39,654 --> 00:54:42,054
I seriously want to eat sushi.

1323
00:54:42,054 --> 00:54:43,624
I'm craving sushi.

1324
00:54:44,654 --> 00:54:46,494
I love pork cutlet as much as Swings does.

1325
00:54:46,494 --> 00:54:47,494
(Seoul Jumbo Pork Cutlet and Hamburger Steak)

1326
00:54:47,494 --> 00:54:48,594
Doesn't this look delicious?

1327
00:54:48,594 --> 00:54:50,024
- I think this one looks tastier.
- Yes.

1328
00:54:50,964 --> 00:54:54,734
(While everyone carefully chooses based on their own criteria)

1329
00:54:54,734 --> 00:54:57,734
There is a huge wait in front of Ho Young's place now too.

1330
00:54:57,734 --> 00:54:58,734
Exactly.

1331
00:54:59,434 --> 00:55:02,174
So is the pork cutlet place the only one without a wait?

1332
00:55:03,574 --> 00:55:05,144
There is no wait here.

1333
00:55:05,144 --> 00:55:06,344
There's no waitlist.

1334
00:55:08,044 --> 00:55:09,944
(Current waitlist, Son of Jeonju: 36 people,)

1335
00:55:09,944 --> 00:55:11,814
(Noodle Shop: 30 people, Seoul Jumbo Pork Cutlet: 0 people)

1336
00:55:11,914 --> 00:55:15,184
I think there's no waiting line here.

1337
00:55:15,654 --> 00:55:17,224
Over there, they have a wait,

1338
00:55:17,224 --> 00:55:18,294
so people are writing down their names.

1339
00:55:18,294 --> 00:55:20,054
(Meanwhile, the two restaurants are packed with waiting customers.)

1340
00:55:20,054 --> 00:55:21,124
Is that so?

1341
00:55:21,124 --> 00:55:22,594
(Kim Hoon's menu)

1342
00:55:22,594 --> 00:55:24,634
- It looks good.
- It must be delicious.

1343
00:55:24,634 --> 00:55:25,794
Should we just go here?

1344
00:55:26,464 --> 00:55:27,804
You don't want to wait, right?

1345
00:55:27,804 --> 00:55:29,764
The line is way too long over there.

1346
00:55:30,504 --> 00:55:32,874
(And a couple currently waiting)

1347
00:55:38,574 --> 00:55:39,944
- Hello.
- Do we have to wait?

1348
00:55:39,944 --> 00:55:41,144
No, you can just come right in.

1349
00:55:41,344 --> 00:55:42,944
One moment, please. How many in your party?

1350
00:55:42,944 --> 00:55:44,554
Two? Please come this way.

1351
00:55:44,784 --> 00:55:46,284
People are giving up on waiting and heading straight...

1352
00:55:46,284 --> 00:55:47,384
to the pork cutlet place.

1353
00:55:48,184 --> 00:55:49,754
Please take the table at the end.

1354
00:55:49,754 --> 00:55:51,354
I'll bring you the menu.

1355
00:55:51,354 --> 00:55:52,454
- How many in your party? Two?
- Two.

1356
00:55:52,454 --> 00:55:54,394
Please take a seat inside.

1357
00:55:54,694 --> 00:55:55,794
Thank you.

1358
00:55:55,794 --> 00:55:57,124
Here's the menu.

1359
00:55:57,124 --> 00:55:59,394
We have a self-serve bar here.

1360
00:55:59,394 --> 00:56:00,734
(Handing over the menu right away and showing them the self-serve bar)

1361
00:56:01,234 --> 00:56:02,504
Let's go.

1362
00:56:02,734 --> 00:56:03,804
It was good, right?

1363
00:56:03,804 --> 00:56:05,704
(As the customers leave at the same time,)

1364
00:56:05,704 --> 00:56:06,874
Excuse me.

1365
00:56:06,874 --> 00:56:09,074
(the register is backed up.)

1366
00:56:09,074 --> 00:56:10,374
- Are you guys ready?
- Yes.

1367
00:56:10,374 --> 00:56:12,744
(Tables that need to be bussed and orders waiting to be taken)

1368
00:56:12,744 --> 00:56:14,044
(Additional customers walking in)

1369
00:56:14,344 --> 00:56:15,344
Do you need a receipt?

1370
00:56:15,614 --> 00:56:17,514
If they just clear these out fast,

1371
00:56:17,514 --> 00:56:19,714
their sales are going to skyrocket.

1372
00:56:21,484 --> 00:56:22,524
(Spotting the backed-up payment line)

1373
00:56:22,524 --> 00:56:24,524
All right. Thank you.

1374
00:56:24,724 --> 00:56:25,724
Are you ready to check out?

1375
00:56:26,194 --> 00:56:27,464
It's number four.

1376
00:56:27,464 --> 00:56:28,524
(He serves the food quickly.)

1377
00:56:28,524 --> 00:56:29,794
- Party of how many?
- Two.

1378
00:56:29,794 --> 00:56:31,364
Two? I'll show you to your seats.

1379
00:56:31,364 --> 00:56:32,834
- Please take the table inside.
- Okay.

1380
00:56:33,564 --> 00:56:35,704
- And one hamburger steak set?
- Yes.

1381
00:56:35,704 --> 00:56:37,474
- I'll have it ready for you.
- Thank you.

1382
00:56:38,204 --> 00:56:40,334
Three people? Please wait a moment.

1383
00:56:41,304 --> 00:56:43,444
I'll get a table ready for three right here.

1384
00:56:43,444 --> 00:56:44,574
Please wait just a moment.

1385
00:56:44,914 --> 00:56:47,344
(We can't let...)

1386
00:56:47,344 --> 00:56:49,084
(our turnover rate fall apart.)

1387
00:56:51,984 --> 00:56:53,614
I'll have the seats ready for you right away.

1388
00:56:54,254 --> 00:56:57,354
(He clears the entire hall all by himself.)

1389
00:56:57,994 --> 00:56:59,324
Please take a seat here.

1390
00:56:59,954 --> 00:57:01,064
Thank you.

1391
00:57:01,064 --> 00:57:03,424
(Then he buses the next table right away.)

1392
00:57:03,424 --> 00:57:04,834
Please sit here.

1393
00:57:04,834 --> 00:57:05,934
This way, please.

1394
00:57:05,934 --> 00:57:08,364
Please take this table. Thank you.

1395
00:57:10,604 --> 00:57:12,134
Okay.

1396
00:57:12,134 --> 00:57:14,504
(The hall is cleared with no waiting customers.)

1397
00:57:14,644 --> 00:57:16,774
Good. Now that we've locked in the turnover, we can win this.

1398
00:57:17,414 --> 00:57:18,644
The longer this drags out, the more it plays in our favour.

1399
00:57:18,644 --> 00:57:20,614
If their waitlists keep piling up, they'll end up coming to us.

1400
00:57:20,644 --> 00:57:21,644
Right?

1401
00:57:22,684 --> 00:57:25,484
Wait, why are there so many people waiting at that noodle shop, though?

1402
00:57:25,484 --> 00:57:27,384
They really need to do something about those tables.

1403
00:57:27,384 --> 00:57:29,124
- Their table turnover is stalled.
- I know.

1404
00:57:29,154 --> 00:57:30,724
A lot of people are waiting.

1405
00:57:31,524 --> 00:57:33,454
Are these people waiting now?

1406
00:57:33,454 --> 00:57:34,924
(10 minutes since the office worker group entered)

1407
00:57:34,924 --> 00:57:36,494
I don't know how long we will have to wait.

1408
00:57:36,964 --> 00:57:38,634
There's a massive line outside,

1409
00:57:38,694 --> 00:57:40,164
but they can't get into our place.

1410
00:57:40,294 --> 00:57:41,734
I know. The tables aren't turning over.

1411
00:57:43,004 --> 00:57:45,634
An entire table is used only for water cups.

1412
00:57:46,204 --> 00:57:48,644
What a waste. I mean those two-seater tables.

1413
00:57:48,644 --> 00:57:50,104
If they get rid of the cups...

1414
00:57:50,474 --> 00:57:52,214
They should've moved those cups and pitchers...

1415
00:57:52,214 --> 00:57:53,874
to a self-serve station.

1416
00:57:54,544 --> 00:57:56,744
Chef Ho Young could have people...

1417
00:57:56,744 --> 00:57:58,054
eat the shaved ice standing up.

1418
00:57:58,284 --> 00:57:59,854
It's actually written over there.

1419
00:57:59,854 --> 00:58:01,684
They're supposed to eat it standing up over there.

1420
00:58:01,984 --> 00:58:03,924
The shaved ice can't be eaten at the dining tables.

1421
00:58:04,254 --> 00:58:05,454
- But people aren't eating it there.
- No.

1422
00:58:05,454 --> 00:58:07,994
They are all eating it at their tables.

1423
00:58:08,564 --> 00:58:10,994
- Yes.
- Injeolmi and shaved ice.

1424
00:58:13,334 --> 00:58:15,404
- I love Injeolmi.
- This is so good.

1425
00:58:15,404 --> 00:58:16,634
(The customers are eating shaved ice at their dining tables.)

1426
00:58:17,034 --> 00:58:18,404
The combination is good.

1427
00:58:18,404 --> 00:58:19,634
(So Ho Young's restaurant is suffering slow turnover.)

1428
00:58:19,634 --> 00:58:21,804
Ho Young's place seems to be getting orders...

1429
00:58:21,804 --> 00:58:23,444
across the whole menu.

1430
00:58:24,274 --> 00:58:25,514
That's the problem.

1431
00:58:25,514 --> 00:58:26,944
- I know.
- It takes a lot of labour.

1432
00:58:26,944 --> 00:58:28,344
- That's what makes things worse.
- It takes so much work,

1433
00:58:28,344 --> 00:58:29,514
but sales aren't that high.

1434
00:58:30,084 --> 00:58:32,754
We should've picked just one direction for the menu.

1435
00:58:33,614 --> 00:58:35,784
The menu is a bit too complicated.

1436
00:58:35,984 --> 00:58:37,554
We have so much variety, you know.

1437
00:58:38,154 --> 00:58:39,454
In the kitchen,

1438
00:58:39,454 --> 00:58:42,124
food was continuously being made,

1439
00:58:42,524 --> 00:58:45,434
but in the hall, Chef Song Hoon had to handle things on his own.

1440
00:58:45,434 --> 00:58:48,034
The fresh pasta and snowflake shaved ice are left, right?

1441
00:58:48,534 --> 00:58:51,204
And on top of that, he had to bus the tables himself.

1442
00:58:51,774 --> 00:58:54,544
- Let me help you with the payment.
- He even had to handle checkout.

1443
00:58:54,544 --> 00:58:55,644
(Song Hoon's work: Serving, busing, cashiering, and making shaved ice)

1444
00:58:55,644 --> 00:58:57,174
Who ordered the shaved ice?

1445
00:58:57,174 --> 00:58:58,274
(Song Hoon's work: Serving, busing, cashiering, and making shaved ice)

1446
00:58:58,444 --> 00:58:59,444
Stay calm.

1447
00:59:00,274 --> 00:59:01,484
From the top.

1448
00:59:01,814 --> 00:59:03,384
Stay calm, Hoon.

1449
00:59:04,454 --> 00:59:07,854
(Stepping out to check on the dining hall)

1450
00:59:10,154 --> 00:59:13,054
(Spotting the shaved ice overflowing)

1451
00:59:13,554 --> 00:59:15,094
(He hurriedly transfers the ice into a fresh bowl.)

1452
00:59:15,094 --> 00:59:17,834
"So this is what was happening."

1453
00:59:18,194 --> 00:59:20,334
"We're definitely shorthanded now."

1454
00:59:20,334 --> 00:59:22,034
That made me realise that.

1455
00:59:22,464 --> 00:59:23,564
How many on the waitlist?

1456
00:59:24,474 --> 00:59:26,004
- Five parties ahead of us.
- Five parties.

1457
00:59:26,174 --> 00:59:28,444
I feel like I should've just eaten that jumbo pork cutlet...

1458
00:59:28,444 --> 00:59:30,144
and hamburger steak over there.

1459
00:59:30,144 --> 00:59:32,444
(The customers are about to leave due to the long wait.)

1460
00:59:32,444 --> 00:59:33,774
They're all going to head over to the pork cutlet place.

1461
00:59:33,774 --> 00:59:35,844
It can't be helped. The wait is just too long.

1462
00:59:37,344 --> 00:59:40,354
(We need to resolve this situation somehow.)

1463
00:59:40,354 --> 00:59:41,354
All right.

1464
00:59:41,924 --> 00:59:43,424
You don't need to come back.

1465
00:59:43,624 --> 00:59:45,294
- What?
- I'll handle things here myself.

1466
00:59:45,294 --> 00:59:46,324
Okay.

1467
00:59:46,324 --> 00:59:47,524
The thing is...

1468
00:59:47,524 --> 00:59:48,564
(Deploying extra staff to the hall to speed up turnover)

1469
00:59:48,564 --> 00:59:49,624
Table turnover is more important now.

1470
00:59:50,164 --> 00:59:51,364
- Hoon.
- Yes?

1471
00:59:51,364 --> 00:59:53,064
Mr. Song is joining you.

1472
00:59:53,064 --> 00:59:55,664
I'll put out all the dishes myself.

1473
00:59:55,764 --> 00:59:56,764
Okay.

1474
00:59:57,064 --> 00:59:58,804
If we don't pull this off now, we're done.

1475
00:59:58,804 --> 01:00:00,534
All right. Understood.

1476
01:00:01,444 --> 01:00:04,074
Chef Song Hoon looked overwhelmed handling the hall alone.

1477
01:00:04,074 --> 01:00:05,944
Even if the food was delayed a bit,

1478
01:00:05,944 --> 01:00:08,614
getting the customers seated came first.

1479
01:00:09,284 --> 01:00:11,884
We just need to push through to the end. Don't worry.

1480
01:00:11,884 --> 01:00:13,054
Let's do this.

1481
01:00:13,954 --> 01:00:15,624
Next party, please come in.

1482
01:00:15,624 --> 01:00:16,654
(Starting to drive up the table turnover)

1483
01:00:16,854 --> 01:00:18,694
We'll seat you as soon as a table opens up.

1484
01:00:18,694 --> 01:00:20,194
One moment, please. How many?

1485
01:00:20,194 --> 01:00:22,394
- Five.
- A table for five?

1486
01:00:22,594 --> 01:00:23,994
- How many in your party?
- It's just me.

1487
01:00:23,994 --> 01:00:26,064
Please sit here. Hello.

1488
01:00:26,864 --> 01:00:28,434
(16 office workers)

1489
01:00:28,434 --> 01:00:29,704
Hello.

1490
01:00:30,764 --> 01:00:32,774
We will have 2 each of numbers 1, 3, and 6, please.

1491
01:00:32,774 --> 01:00:33,804
Two and four.

1492
01:00:33,804 --> 01:00:35,474
- Two of each of these?
- Yes.

1493
01:00:35,474 --> 01:00:37,104
Numbers 2, 4, and 5.

1494
01:00:37,474 --> 01:00:39,514
One pasta, one risotto...

1495
01:00:39,514 --> 01:00:42,214
One mianbao xia and a set of cold udon and assorted sushi.

1496
01:00:42,844 --> 01:00:44,044
Is this not allowed?

1497
01:00:44,044 --> 01:00:45,454
Not at all. It's fine.

1498
01:00:45,454 --> 01:00:46,984
(153.50 dollars in total)

1499
01:00:46,984 --> 01:00:50,084
Four bibim and three cold udon?

1500
01:00:50,384 --> 01:00:52,154
Two more orders of sushi need to go out.

1501
01:00:52,154 --> 01:00:54,224
- How many?
- Three in total.

1502
01:00:54,224 --> 01:00:55,964
- Three for sushi?
- Yes.

1503
01:00:55,964 --> 01:00:57,094
(Orders crash into the kitchen with just two people.)

1504
01:00:57,294 --> 01:00:59,734
(Grabbing a handful of sushi rice)

1505
01:01:00,864 --> 01:01:06,234
(Speedily knocking out three sushi sets)

1506
01:01:11,844 --> 01:01:14,014
- Here's the sushi.
- Thank you.

1507
01:01:14,014 --> 01:01:15,014
(Sushi goes out first.)

1508
01:01:15,014 --> 01:01:17,114
(Plating udon)

1509
01:01:17,114 --> 01:01:19,754
(Frying shrimp)

1510
01:01:19,754 --> 01:01:22,124
(Garnishing)

1511
01:01:22,124 --> 01:01:24,254
(Pouring broth)

1512
01:01:24,624 --> 01:01:28,194
(He knocks everything out at high speed.)

1513
01:01:28,724 --> 01:01:30,024
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

1514
01:01:30,024 --> 01:01:31,164
Enjoy it.

1515
01:01:33,734 --> 01:01:34,734
(Exclaiming)

1516
01:01:34,734 --> 01:01:35,764
It's good.

1517
01:01:38,204 --> 01:01:41,344
(Exclaiming)

1518
01:01:41,374 --> 01:01:42,744
It tastes good.

1519
01:01:45,114 --> 01:01:46,244
It's so tender.

1520
01:01:47,174 --> 01:01:49,644
(Homemade cold udon)

1521
01:01:49,644 --> 01:01:50,984
(Exclaiming)

1522
01:01:50,984 --> 01:01:51,984
Is it good?

1523
01:01:51,984 --> 01:01:53,314
(Nodding)

1524
01:01:53,314 --> 01:01:55,124
I don't usually care much for udon.

1525
01:01:55,384 --> 01:01:57,724
But the broth and the noodles here are really good.

1526
01:01:57,724 --> 01:01:58,754
Right. It's delicious.

1527
01:01:58,754 --> 01:02:00,494
(Homemade noodles make a difference. The udon is insane.)

1528
01:02:00,494 --> 01:02:01,724
(The wasabi packs a punch, but that was genuinely good sushi.)

1529
01:02:01,724 --> 01:02:05,234
(Rave reviews make up for the painful wait.)

1530
01:02:05,464 --> 01:02:08,234
The customer ratings are being updated in real time.

1531
01:02:09,634 --> 01:02:14,374
Jung Ho Young and Song Hoon have climbed to first place in ratings.

1532
01:02:16,174 --> 01:02:18,514
Hey! Song Hoon, Jung Ho Young!

1533
01:02:18,944 --> 01:02:21,914
Ho Young's team nailed the flavour profile. It's good.

1534
01:02:22,544 --> 01:02:24,114
At least the ratings look great.

1535
01:02:24,114 --> 01:02:25,484
- Who?
- It's us.

1536
01:02:26,284 --> 01:02:29,184
- Third place, Lee Sung Hoon.
- Let it break four.

1537
01:02:29,184 --> 01:02:30,554
It's 3.86.

1538
01:02:30,554 --> 01:02:31,654
Darn it.

1539
01:02:31,654 --> 01:02:33,854
(3rd place: Lee Sung Hoon, 3.86)

1540
01:02:33,854 --> 01:02:35,964
We're an absolute mess now.

1541
01:02:36,964 --> 01:02:39,994
My gosh. They are falling so far behind. What do they do?

1542
01:02:40,634 --> 01:02:43,464
(Lee Sung Hoon's restaurant still has a massive waiting line.)

1543
01:02:45,274 --> 01:02:46,934
Tae Hee, we have to clear our waitlist.

1544
01:02:46,934 --> 01:02:48,204
We need to keep it going.

1545
01:02:49,144 --> 01:02:50,544
I felt so rushed.

1546
01:02:50,544 --> 01:02:52,944
We targeted the office worker group,

1547
01:02:53,114 --> 01:02:55,844
but many of them didn't show up because of the slow table turnover.

1548
01:02:56,084 --> 01:02:59,254
We pushed hard to get dishes out as fast as possible.

1549
01:02:59,384 --> 01:03:05,154
(Serving Korean melon salad and steak)

1550
01:03:05,254 --> 01:03:06,724
(Flustered)

1551
01:03:06,724 --> 01:03:09,094
- What's that?
- They skipped this one.

1552
01:03:09,094 --> 01:03:10,624
(They skipped this dish.)

1553
01:03:10,624 --> 01:03:12,994
True. And this one is this.

1554
01:03:12,994 --> 01:03:14,934
That's the salad. That's this one.

1555
01:03:14,934 --> 01:03:15,934
(Steak and salad are served before the makguksu.)

1556
01:03:16,164 --> 01:03:17,234
Thank you.

1557
01:03:17,234 --> 01:03:19,804
(At another table, bracken hangover soup is being served.)

1558
01:03:19,804 --> 01:03:22,774
This is... You didn't get this one?

1559
01:03:23,244 --> 01:03:24,314
- Number...
- Numbers 4 and 5.

1560
01:03:24,314 --> 01:03:25,574
Okay.

1561
01:03:25,574 --> 01:03:27,314
I'll bring it right away.

1562
01:03:27,744 --> 01:03:29,144
(Without serving the steak and Korean melon salad,)

1563
01:03:29,144 --> 01:03:30,644
(he gave them the bracken hangover soup first.)

1564
01:03:30,884 --> 01:03:32,754
(Setting it aside)

1565
01:03:32,754 --> 01:03:35,024
Can you make 2 salads 1st?

1566
01:03:35,154 --> 01:03:36,924
Tae Hee, I'll take care of it. Just tell me what to do.

1567
01:03:36,924 --> 01:03:38,354
- Steak for 3.
- Steak for 3?

1568
01:03:38,494 --> 01:03:39,494
On a single plate?

1569
01:03:39,494 --> 01:03:43,324
For a course meal, pacing and sequence are crucial.

1570
01:03:43,394 --> 01:03:45,234
And we were completely failing at them.

1571
01:03:45,764 --> 01:03:48,134
(For pacing and sequence,)

1572
01:03:48,604 --> 01:03:50,964
(communication between the hall and kitchen is essential.)

1573
01:03:51,304 --> 01:03:53,204
Tae Hee, I'll plate the food, so you go help out in the hall.

1574
01:03:53,634 --> 01:03:55,604
- Four servings?
- Yes.

1575
01:03:55,604 --> 01:03:57,104
And figure out what else is needed.

1576
01:03:57,504 --> 01:04:00,544
Sung Hoon is in chaos from the rush.

1577
01:04:00,814 --> 01:04:03,114
He tells him to get out there and clear the tables. It's crazy.

1578
01:04:03,584 --> 01:04:06,184
(Yu Tae Hee is deployed full-time to the hall.)

1579
01:04:06,184 --> 01:04:08,224
The role Tae Hee had was crucial.

1580
01:04:08,224 --> 01:04:09,624
He had to back up the hall...

1581
01:04:09,624 --> 01:04:11,394
and also finished up the dishes,

1582
01:04:11,494 --> 01:04:13,124
so the lead naturally shifted over.

1583
01:04:13,694 --> 01:04:16,464
(Quickly finishing up the clean-up)

1584
01:04:16,464 --> 01:04:18,094
- I'll seat customers.
- Go ahead.

1585
01:04:18,934 --> 01:04:20,794
(The moment a party of 4 walks in)

1586
01:04:20,794 --> 01:04:22,234
Tartare for four.

1587
01:04:22,704 --> 01:04:24,634
(Rapid call-out)

1588
01:04:24,734 --> 01:04:27,404
- How many makguksu do you need?
- Two for now.

1589
01:04:27,874 --> 01:04:29,844
Excuse me. Here's your tartare.

1590
01:04:30,604 --> 01:04:32,314
Thank you so much for waiting.

1591
01:04:32,314 --> 01:04:33,844
You can take a seat inside.

1592
01:04:33,844 --> 01:04:34,914
(Table turnover resumes.)

1593
01:04:35,714 --> 01:04:38,354
Isn't Sung Hoon's strength staying very calm, though?

1594
01:04:39,184 --> 01:04:41,014
Sometimes he stays too calm even when he shouldn't be.

1595
01:04:41,014 --> 01:04:42,554
- Really?
- Even when he needs to hurry,

1596
01:04:42,554 --> 01:04:43,724
- he tends to stay calm.
- I see.

1597
01:04:44,854 --> 01:04:46,094
But I think he can pull it off now.

1598
01:04:46,094 --> 01:04:49,494
Once the tables turn one round, the tides will completely turn.

1599
01:04:49,794 --> 01:04:54,404
(Checking on the progress of the courses)

1600
01:04:55,664 --> 01:04:58,334
They're walking by to check our eating speed.

1601
01:04:59,534 --> 01:05:01,604
To see if we've finished.

1602
01:05:02,374 --> 01:05:04,774
It's a course meal, so the next dish comes out when we finish.

1603
01:05:06,444 --> 01:05:07,674
Did we eat too fast?

1604
01:05:09,044 --> 01:05:10,444
I'm looking forward to the tiramisu now.

1605
01:05:11,014 --> 01:05:12,054
Tiramisu?

1606
01:05:13,214 --> 01:05:14,854
I bet the tiramisu is going to be insanely delicious.

1607
01:05:14,854 --> 01:05:16,484
(What will the highly anticipated tiramisu taste like?)

1608
01:05:16,654 --> 01:05:18,394
I'm the most critical when it comes to baked goods.

1609
01:05:19,994 --> 01:05:23,494
(The comment from a customer with strict standards for bread?)

1610
01:05:23,494 --> 01:05:25,394
(Exclaiming)

1611
01:05:26,234 --> 01:05:27,394
I like the tiramisu.

1612
01:05:28,064 --> 01:05:30,504
I liked the makguksu and the Korean melon salad best.

1613
01:05:31,674 --> 01:05:33,174
The tiramisu is delicious too.

1614
01:05:34,504 --> 01:05:36,004
The coffee aroma is so good.

1615
01:05:36,004 --> 01:05:38,244
(Sung Hoon overheard it while clearing a table.)

1616
01:05:39,344 --> 01:05:40,674
Do we have enough tiramisu left?

1617
01:05:40,774 --> 01:05:41,814
Yes. We have a lot.

1618
01:05:44,454 --> 01:05:46,984
Excuse me. You seemed to enjoy the tiramisu.

1619
01:05:47,884 --> 01:05:49,084
- Thank you.
- How did you know?

1620
01:05:49,484 --> 01:05:50,954
Thank you so much for enjoying your meal.

1621
01:05:50,954 --> 01:05:51,954
(Complimentary tiramisu on the house)

1622
01:05:52,024 --> 01:05:54,354
We've got power. One tiramisu per person.

1623
01:06:00,334 --> 01:06:03,464
Here are the current sales rankings.

1624
01:06:03,864 --> 01:06:06,104
First place, Lee Sung Hoon.

1625
01:06:07,234 --> 01:06:09,304
- Second place, Kim Hoon.
- I'll show you to your seats soon.

1626
01:06:10,504 --> 01:06:12,974
Third place, Jung Ho Young.

1627
01:06:13,314 --> 01:06:16,084
Mianbao xia, risotto, pasta.

1628
01:06:16,344 --> 01:06:18,484
- Please take the win.
- Please, Lee Sung Hoon.

1629
01:06:18,854 --> 01:06:20,454
- Even though we lost...
- Please...

1630
01:06:20,914 --> 01:06:22,024
Though we lost to him...

1631
01:06:22,024 --> 01:06:25,154
(Current time)

1632
01:06:25,824 --> 01:06:27,794
Keep walking.

1633
01:06:28,024 --> 01:06:29,064
Walk.

1634
01:06:30,124 --> 01:06:31,194
It's here.

1635
01:06:32,564 --> 01:06:35,304
Where? I smell something delicious.

1636
01:06:36,264 --> 01:06:37,874
The sixth target group...

1637
01:06:38,704 --> 01:06:40,474
is families with children.

1638
01:06:41,404 --> 01:06:45,314
(Family customers with children of elementary school age or younger)

1639
01:06:45,314 --> 01:06:47,244
They're here. Families.

1640
01:06:47,944 --> 01:06:49,014
- They're here.
- The families are here.

1641
01:06:49,344 --> 01:06:50,944
- It's the last group.
- They're the last group, right?

1642
01:06:51,514 --> 01:06:52,814
I'm hungry.

1643
01:06:53,354 --> 01:06:54,924
I'm starving.

1644
01:06:55,824 --> 01:06:57,624
Let's go over there, Dad.

1645
01:06:58,124 --> 01:06:59,554
(Which restaurant...)

1646
01:06:59,554 --> 01:07:00,554
What's that?

1647
01:07:00,894 --> 01:07:01,924
Is it available?

1648
01:07:02,224 --> 01:07:03,264
Let's go and check.

1649
01:07:03,264 --> 01:07:04,594
(will families with kids choose the most?)

1650
01:07:06,234 --> 01:07:10,834
(Customers heading straight in as soon as they arrive)

1651
01:07:12,734 --> 01:07:15,204
(Waiting in line)

1652
01:07:15,204 --> 01:07:17,144
We're not in this line. You can go right in.

1653
01:07:17,144 --> 01:07:18,374
Can we go in?

1654
01:07:20,544 --> 01:07:22,344
- Yes. Let's go.
- Nice.

1655
01:07:22,344 --> 01:07:23,644
They go to the pork cutlet place.

1656
01:07:24,484 --> 01:07:25,614
They don't hesitate at all.

1657
01:07:25,614 --> 01:07:26,654
(Entering without a second thought)

1658
01:07:26,714 --> 01:07:27,924
They head straight in.

1659
01:07:29,184 --> 01:07:30,854
- Pork cutlet!
- They're so cute.

1660
01:07:30,854 --> 01:07:32,624
- They don't look anywhere else.
- Pork cutlet.

1661
01:07:32,694 --> 01:07:34,564
For pork cutlet, they just go straight in.

1662
01:07:35,324 --> 01:07:37,464
I think the other kids will head over here too.

1663
01:07:38,064 --> 01:07:39,134
Do you want to eat this?

1664
01:07:39,434 --> 01:07:40,434
I want this.

1665
01:07:40,434 --> 01:07:42,334
- Do you want it?
- Let's go in. Come here.

1666
01:07:43,334 --> 01:07:45,234
- Shall we go here?
- Where?

1667
01:07:45,734 --> 01:07:47,704
Dad, I want to eat a pork cutlet.

1668
01:07:48,274 --> 01:07:49,874
They also have ice cream.

1669
01:07:49,874 --> 01:07:51,314
Yes. They give it out for free.

1670
01:07:51,774 --> 01:07:54,444
If you eat your meal well, they'll give you ice cream.

1671
01:07:54,944 --> 01:07:57,614
(Customers are rushing in right from the start.)

1672
01:07:58,054 --> 01:08:01,324
(It even generates a waiting line.)

1673
01:08:01,854 --> 01:08:04,054
- It's guaranteed.
- Pork cutlet!

1674
01:08:04,054 --> 01:08:05,254
All the kids are having pork cutlet.

1675
01:08:05,294 --> 01:08:06,854
The menu here is too much for children.

1676
01:08:06,854 --> 01:08:07,994
Right. It won't work.

1677
01:08:07,994 --> 01:08:09,194
(The neighbouring restaurants' menus are too much for kids.)

1678
01:08:09,624 --> 01:08:11,094
- Do you want to eat this?
- Yes.

1679
01:08:11,094 --> 01:08:13,364
(An unprecedented waitlist forms at the pork cutlet restaurant.)

1680
01:08:14,194 --> 01:08:15,734
Welcome.

1681
01:08:15,804 --> 01:08:17,404
- Welcome.
- Hello. How many in your party?

1682
01:08:17,734 --> 01:08:19,104
Please wait a moment.

1683
01:08:19,104 --> 01:08:20,134
One moment, please.

1684
01:08:20,204 --> 01:08:22,444
If you wait just a moment, I'll help seat you.

1685
01:08:22,444 --> 01:08:23,474
(Customers are walking in one after another.)

1686
01:08:23,474 --> 01:08:24,914
One moment. Please be careful.

1687
01:08:24,914 --> 01:08:26,014
How many in your party?

1688
01:08:26,374 --> 01:08:28,884
(Mesmerized eyes)

1689
01:08:29,014 --> 01:08:30,414
Thank you. How many?

1690
01:08:30,614 --> 01:08:32,484
- Four.
- Four? Wait a moment.

1691
01:08:32,814 --> 01:08:33,914
(Even an 8-person family enters.)

1692
01:08:33,914 --> 01:08:36,054
I'll show you to your seats. Thank you.

1693
01:08:36,784 --> 01:08:38,654
(A massive boom for the pork cutlet place)

1694
01:08:38,654 --> 01:08:40,094
Mom, what is this?

1695
01:08:41,154 --> 01:08:42,964
Excuse me. I'll get you a high chair.

1696
01:08:43,024 --> 01:08:45,234
Please tick the boxes and hand it to me.

1697
01:08:45,464 --> 01:08:46,794
He's taking out a high chair.

1698
01:08:46,794 --> 01:08:47,864
- It's game over.
- A high chair.

1699
01:08:47,864 --> 01:08:49,364
The high chair is out.

1700
01:08:50,364 --> 01:08:53,374
(The high chairs sat tucked away in the corner since morning.)

1701
01:08:53,904 --> 01:08:57,904
(It's finally having its moment to shine.)

1702
01:08:58,944 --> 01:09:00,774
We have parties of three on the waitlist now.

1703
01:09:02,214 --> 01:09:04,084
- We have one pork cutlet to serve.
- Okay.

1704
01:09:05,554 --> 01:09:09,224
(Orders are piling up as fast as the rush of customers.)

1705
01:09:13,924 --> 01:09:15,024
Five pork cutlets.

1706
01:09:15,894 --> 01:09:18,234
(He knocks out orders alone,)

1707
01:09:18,234 --> 01:09:21,564
(no matter the volume.)

1708
01:09:21,804 --> 01:09:22,964
(Cabbage)

1709
01:09:23,334 --> 01:09:24,334
(Corn)

1710
01:09:24,904 --> 01:09:26,134
(Pork cutlet)

1711
01:09:26,134 --> 01:09:27,934
- Can these go out now?
- Yes.

1712
01:09:28,974 --> 01:09:30,774
Jong In is doing everything by himself.

1713
01:09:30,874 --> 01:09:32,814
That’s practically a one-man circus from Kim Jong In now.

1714
01:09:33,714 --> 01:09:35,984
He's knocking everything out in the kitchen all on his own.

1715
01:09:37,614 --> 01:09:40,054
I should open a restaurant with Jong In.

1716
01:09:40,914 --> 01:09:43,524
He works so well on his own.

1717
01:09:47,054 --> 01:09:48,994
(Turning on the gas burner with his knee)

1718
01:09:49,124 --> 01:09:52,564
Did you notice Jong In just bent his knee?

1719
01:09:53,064 --> 01:09:56,204
No. He turned on the gas with his knee.

1720
01:09:56,364 --> 01:09:57,864
It was the burner.

1721
01:09:57,934 --> 01:09:59,304
That's how he turns up the burner.

1722
01:09:59,304 --> 01:10:00,904
- Was it for the burner?
- Yes.

1723
01:10:00,904 --> 01:10:02,174
He turned it up like that.

1724
01:10:03,004 --> 01:10:05,144
Jong In is working hard and killing it.

1725
01:10:06,274 --> 01:10:08,444
- Don't let your guard down yet.
- Let's not get ahead of ourselves.

1726
01:10:09,014 --> 01:10:10,844
Customer ratings can flip everything upside down.

1727
01:10:12,454 --> 01:10:14,654
Yes. Here's your food.

1728
01:10:14,654 --> 01:10:16,184
(Serving completed in no time)

1729
01:10:16,624 --> 01:10:17,924
- Eat up.
- Okay.

1730
01:10:19,994 --> 01:10:23,564
(Next to two kids devouring their pork cutlets)

1731
01:10:24,164 --> 01:10:25,434
It looks unique.

1732
01:10:25,434 --> 01:10:27,134
(He's crushing the soba all by himself.)

1733
01:10:27,234 --> 01:10:28,964
It has lasagna in it.

1734
01:10:31,204 --> 01:10:32,474
- Geon Woo.
- Yes?

1735
01:10:32,474 --> 01:10:33,934
- Were you hungry?
- Yes.

1736
01:10:34,504 --> 01:10:36,574
He's finishing the whole soba by himself.

1737
01:10:39,314 --> 01:10:41,914
(Chugging the broth down)

1738
01:10:42,244 --> 01:10:44,014
Geon Woo seems to like the soba most.

1739
01:10:44,014 --> 01:10:45,484
It turns out this place is a soba hotspot.

1740
01:10:45,614 --> 01:10:46,784
Would you like some more soba?

1741
01:10:46,784 --> 01:10:48,184
- Pardon?
- Would you like some more soba?

1742
01:10:48,184 --> 01:10:49,454
Do you want some more?

1743
01:10:50,524 --> 01:10:51,794
- Just a little, please.
- Okay.

1744
01:10:51,894 --> 01:10:53,194
- Do you like it, Geon Woo?
- Yes.

1745
01:10:53,194 --> 01:10:54,554
(Nodding)

1746
01:10:56,094 --> 01:10:57,124
I'll get you another bowl of soba.

1747
01:10:57,124 --> 01:10:58,434
Thank you.

1748
01:10:59,834 --> 01:11:01,034
He got you more soba.

1749
01:11:01,034 --> 01:11:02,264
(Another bowl of soba on the house for the kid who eats so well)

1750
01:11:02,534 --> 01:11:04,834
(Another table of a family with a kid)

1751
01:11:05,204 --> 01:11:08,474
(He focuses on his pork cutlet.)

1752
01:11:08,804 --> 01:11:09,804
Do you like it?

1753
01:11:09,804 --> 01:11:11,344
It's great that Do Hun likes the food.

1754
01:11:12,714 --> 01:11:13,844
Did we make the right choice with this?

1755
01:11:14,014 --> 01:11:15,584
This is Do Hun's favourite menu.

1756
01:11:16,184 --> 01:11:17,884
For family customers, this place is number one.

1757
01:11:20,754 --> 01:11:24,324
(10 minutes before the last call)

1758
01:11:24,854 --> 01:11:28,664
(Lee Sung Hoon's restaurant checks the waitlist.)

1759
01:11:28,864 --> 01:11:30,464
Is Ms. Lee Chae Yeon here?

1760
01:11:31,594 --> 01:11:33,194
Ms. Lee Chae Yeon?

1761
01:11:34,334 --> 01:11:36,064
Is Mr. Lee Jung Hun here?

1762
01:11:36,064 --> 01:11:37,734
Mr. Lee Jung Hun?

1763
01:11:37,734 --> 01:11:39,534
(The customers who had been waiting left for other restaurants.)

1764
01:11:39,774 --> 01:11:41,444
- It's over. They're all gone.
- Is it over?

1765
01:11:41,444 --> 01:11:42,604
- They left?
- Yes.

1766
01:11:43,074 --> 01:11:45,244
- No one on the waitlist?
- No one's waiting.

1767
01:11:49,514 --> 01:11:52,654
Here are the current sales rankings.

1768
01:11:53,754 --> 01:11:55,054
First place.

1769
01:11:58,054 --> 01:11:59,124
Lee Sung Hoon.

1770
01:12:00,154 --> 01:12:01,694
Let's just focus on what we have to do now.

1771
01:12:02,224 --> 01:12:04,524
(Unshakeable 1st place in sales until the final target group)

1772
01:12:05,034 --> 01:12:06,434
- My goodness.
- My goodness.

1773
01:12:06,994 --> 01:12:09,104
- It's because of the price.
- The price is high.

1774
01:12:09,504 --> 01:12:11,574
Once they settle the bill and leave, sales just spike instantly.

1775
01:12:12,234 --> 01:12:14,134
Because 10 people easily make it 350 dollars.

1776
01:12:14,974 --> 01:12:16,674
They don't even need high table turnover here.

1777
01:12:17,644 --> 01:12:20,014
Just that amount easily pulls in nearly 500 to 600 dollars.

1778
01:12:20,614 --> 01:12:22,744
If they score well on the ratings, it will be enough.

1779
01:12:22,744 --> 01:12:25,154
The check average per person is almost double.

1780
01:12:25,914 --> 01:12:27,984
Please double-check if there's anything missing.

1781
01:12:27,984 --> 01:12:28,984
Okay.

1782
01:12:28,984 --> 01:12:30,484
There are no new walk-ins now,

1783
01:12:31,524 --> 01:12:32,794
so we can take our time.

1784
01:12:32,794 --> 01:12:34,394
No. For now,

1785
01:12:34,394 --> 01:12:36,894
please check on the customers to see if we missed anything.

1786
01:12:37,694 --> 01:12:39,794
They seem to hate waiting. Let's get the food out quickly.

1787
01:12:41,134 --> 01:12:42,704
But their customer ratings...

1788
01:12:42,804 --> 01:12:45,204
We never know what they got for customer ratings.

1789
01:12:46,134 --> 01:12:48,604
(Currently, Jung Ho Young is in 1st with 4.38 customer ratings.)

1790
01:12:49,204 --> 01:12:53,014
(Jung Ho Young's restaurant still has a line.)

1791
01:12:53,674 --> 01:12:55,684
They're still packed.

1792
01:12:57,084 --> 01:13:00,854
(The restaurant is still packed.)

1793
01:13:01,214 --> 01:13:02,884
Still, I got the highest customer ratings.

1794
01:13:04,124 --> 01:13:05,554
Another risotto.

1795
01:13:05,554 --> 01:13:07,124
